		{
			"name": "2. Brownfield - V1 baseline, then V2 cutover",
			"description": "Tests V1 first as the pre-existing baseline system, then represents 'a commit that activates V2' by creating the same link on V2, and verifies the Gateway resolves the new V2 code correctly on the very first try -- and still correctly after a direct read against V2, too. Maps to the Day 2 scenario documented in ARCHITECTURE.md (V1-only baseline, then V2 cutover). Used to reproduce a cache-as-index defect here (see AI_USAGE_LOG.md and ARCHITECTURE.md section 13); DynamicShortCodeRoutingFilter no longer depends on a Redis cache at all, so this folder now asserts the fixed behavior rather than tolerating the old one. Run '0. Auth' first.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Create short link (V1 - the pre-existing system)",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/urls",
							"host": [
								"{{gatewayUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v1",
								"urls"
							]
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"longUrl\": \"https://www.anthropic.com/news\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"description": "Goes through the Gateway, not straight to V1 - k3d's k3d-config.yaml only maps host ports 8081/8082/8084 (Keycloak/Gateway/V2), so a direct V1 port is not guaranteed to exist under Option B. The Gateway forwards /api/v1/** to V1_LEGACY_MONOLITH_URL unconditionally (no cache/index dependency, unlike the V1/V2 redirect dispatch below), so this works identically under docker-compose (Option A) and k3d (Option B). Confirmed against a live k3d cluster: POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/urls returns 201 with a real shortCode."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('V1 create returns 201', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('Response has a shortCode', function () {",
									"    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('shortCode');",
									"});",
									"if (body.shortCode) {",
									"    pm.collectionVariables.set('bfV1ShortCode', body.shortCode);",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Redirect via Gateway (routes to V1, as V2 has nothing yet)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/{{bfV1ShortCode}}",
							"host": [
								"{{gatewayUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"{{bfV1ShortCode}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Confirms the Gateway's V1 fallback path works for a code V2 has never seen - this is the Day 1 baseline behavior, before any V2 cutover."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Gateway falls through to V1 and returns 301', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(301);",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"protocolProfileBehavior": {
						"followRedirects": false
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "'Cutover commit': create the same link on V2",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							},
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{v2Url}}/api/v2/urls",
							"host": [
								"{{v2Url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"v2",
								"urls"
							]
						},
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"longUrl\": \"https://www.anthropic.com/news\"\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"description": "Represents 'a commit that activates V2': from this point on, the system has a V2-side entry that did not exist when the Gateway request above was made. This models the documented Day 2 scenario in ARCHITECTURE.md (V1-only baseline, then V2 cutover)."
					},
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('V2 create returns 201', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"if (body.shortCode) {",
